Complete Startup Guide
Step 1: Start Docker Containers (PostgreSQL + Redis)
Open Terminal 1 (PowerShell or Command Prompt as Administrator):

bash
cd C:\Users\paulo\Documents\cloud-cost-optimization-hub
docker-compose up -d
Wait about 30 seconds for the databases to initialize.

Verify they're running:

bash
docker ps
You should see both ccoh-postgres and ccoh-redis running.

Step 2: Start the Backend
Open Terminal 2:

bash
cd C:\Users\paulo\Documents\cloud-cost-optimization-hub\backend
go run cmd/api/main.go
Leave this terminal running. You should see:

text
Starting Cloud Cost Optimization Hub API Server
Database connected successfully
Server listening on port 8080
Step 3: Start the Frontend
Open Terminal 3:

bash
cd C:\Users\paulo\Documents\cloud-cost-optimization-hub\frontend
npm run dev
Leave this terminal running. You should see:

text
▲ Next.js 15.5.15
- Local:        http://localhost:3000
Step 4: Access the Application
Open your browser to: http://localhost:3000

