Stopping Everything
When you're done:

Terminal 3: Press Ctrl + C to stop frontend

Terminal 2: Press Ctrl + C to stop backend

Terminal 1: Run docker-compose down to stop databases

Troubleshooting
If port 8080 is already in use:
bash
# Check what's using port 8080
netstat -ano | findstr :8080

# Kill the process (replace PID with the number from above)
taskkill /PID [PID_NUMBER] /F
If port 3000 is already in use:
bash
netstat -ano | findstr :3000
taskkill /PID [PID_NUMBER] /F
If database connection fails:
Make sure Docker is running and containers are up:

bash
docker-compose restart postgres redis
If migrations need to be run again:
bash
cd C:\Users\paulo\Documents\cloud-cost-optimization-hub\backend
go run cmd/migrator/main.go -direction up
Once both are running, go to http://localhost:3000 and log in. Then navigate to http://localhost:3000/accounts to add your AWS account!